# useState with Object

```jsx
const [user, setUser] = useState({
  name: "Najim",
  age: 21,
});
```

Display:

```jsx
<h1>{user.name}</h1>
<h1>{user.age}</h1>
```

Update:

```jsx
setUser({
  ...user,
  age: 22,
});
```

Why use ...user?

Because React replaces the whole object.

Wrong:

```jsx
setUser({ age: 22 });
```

Result:

```jsx
{
  age: 22
}
```

name gets deleted.

